Below is a proposed plan for creating separate GitHub repositories for each of the major systems in the EternaFX Collaborative Platform. This modular approach will allow you to manage, develop, and deploy each system independently while maintaining a unified overall framework. Each repository includes its own configuration, data, documentation, source code (organized by functional modules), tests, scripts, and notebooks.


---

1. EternaFX-AGI Repository

Purpose: Contains all AGI (Artificial General Intelligence) components, including core decision-making, memory management, reasoning, and ethical governance.

Proposed Structure:

EternaFX-AGI/
├── config/             
│   └── config.yaml        # Environment variables, API keys, etc.
├── data/                
│   ├── datasets/          # Raw and preprocessed AGI-related datasets
│   └── checkpoints/       # Saved model weights and states
├── docs/                
│   ├── API.md             # API documentation
│   ├── research_papers/   # Relevant research references
│   └── diagrams/          # Architecture and workflow diagrams
├── src/                 
│   ├── agi/
│   │   ├── core/
│   │   │   ├── proto_conscious_agi.py
│   │   │   └── curiosity_driven_agi.py
│   │   ├── memory/
│   │   │   └── memory_manager.py
│   │   ├── reasoning/
│   │   │   └── problem_solver.py
│   │   └── ethics/
│   │       └── ethics_manager.py
│   └── main.py            # Entry point for AGI simulations
├── tests/                 
│   └── test_agi.py        # Unit and integration tests for AGI modules
├── scripts/               
│   └── deploy.sh          # Deployment scripts and automation tasks
├── notebooks/             
│   └── agi_prototyping.ipynb  # Jupyter notebooks for prototyping AGI ideas
└── README.md              # Overview and setup instructions


